  "what_the_study_did": "This chapter reviews the anatomy of the extrapyramidal system and discusses several naturally occurring and experimental models that target the mammalian (nonhuman) extrapyramidal system, focusing on the concordance between clinical signs, neurochemical changes, and neuropathology between animals and people.",
  "what_it_found": "The chapter discusses various agents and syndromes affecting the extrapyramidal system, with a focus on animal models used to understand toxicity and pathogenesis, and highlights yellowstar thistle poisoning in horses as a spontaneous cause of parkinsonism in animals.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In most cases, animals are used as experimental models to improve our understanding of the toxicity and pathogenesis of these agents.",
      "topic": "Animal models"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Another agent discussed in this chapter, yellowstar thistle poisoning in horses, however, represents an important spontaneous cause of parkinsonism that naturally occurs in animals.",
      "topic": "Spontaneous animal parkinsonism"
    },
    {
      "quote": "The central focus of the chapter is on animal models, especially the concordance between clinical signs, neurochemical changes, and neuropathology between animals and people.",
      "topic": "Focus on concordance"
    }
  ]
